And I feel like it doesn't really change much in that.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.000
It's not like a terrible way.

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:37.260
It's not like terribly boring.

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:40.280
It's just that you get it right away when you boot it up.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.480
You kind of get it from the first five minutes.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.840
And then it's not going to change too much more after that.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:46.800
Right. It's auto-scrolling.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:51.500
You're going through waves of enemies, tanks, other flying aircrafts.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:56.440
Sometimes you can pretend that the people in the houses are attacking you to justify your reason for attacking them.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:58.700
And you're just going through that.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:04.120
And like Sean, either you or Sean mentioned, it's slow-paced.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:07.160
It doesn't move as fast as some of our other shmups.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.520
Joe said it first. Okay, great.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:10.340
I like the idea that you said either you or Sean.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.020
I guess if we're talking to the listeners, like either you or Sean.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.640
One of the listeners might have suggested that the game is slow.

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:19.260
But then also it's worth noting that there's only four stages.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.760
Yeah. Like four stages.

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:25.720
Like, you know, it's stage one, stage two, stage three, stage four.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:29.200
And then stage five, which they do call it stage five, is stage two again.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:30.540
Stage two again?

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:31.580
Yeah. That's interesting.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:35.320
Yeah. It's not a – they don't want you to feel like it's actually a loop.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:40.240
So like stage five is two, then three, then four, then I think three, two, four.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:41.240
Like they change it up.

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:43.180
Interesting. But it's always the same thing.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.180
Yeah, I only played as long as it could keep my attention.

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.960
But I guess it wasn't long enough.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.460
Yeah, so you didn't get through all four stages.

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:56.140
I feel like I got four stages through.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.640
Yeah, and it didn't probably feel too much like a finale.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:01.320
No. Yeah. That's what I'm going to get at too.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:04.160
It's like the game doesn't want you to know it's ended.

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.360
So it just keeps dragging stages.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.060
At least increasing the number of stages.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.660
If we could, like to talk about the manual for a minute.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.080
Yeah. So maybe you guys break –

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.020
We'll get into this propaganda.

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:16.620
Yeah, break out your manuals.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:18.120
Breaking them out. All right.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.080
So there's nothing like exceptional about this manual.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:28.720
But I do like the scene that's page four and five where it kind of like tries to lay out like a –

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.740
You know, this is the entire story you're going to get out of Tiger Heli.

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:35.800
There's nothing in the game that really like alludes to anything bigger happening.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:39.300
So all of it is like in this small little story here.

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:44.340
So they have the place, which is the mega fortress of the terrorist regime.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:47.620
Now, I don't know about you guys, but I didn't get that vibe.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:50.040
Yeah, it's just the –

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:50.900
The mega fortress.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:52.500
It's a suburban area.

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.460
And then you just cross into the water.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:59.120
And, yeah, there's ships and stuff because you've attacked them.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:00.720
Yeah, all those just like –

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.080
All those like houses with like nice yards and stuff.

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.140
Is that the mega fortress?

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:06.800
That's the mega fortress. Maybe you don't start in the mega fortress.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:11.200
Oh, you're on your way. But it does seem weird that the manual fails to call that out, right?

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:14.640
Like you start – maybe that's our home country we started.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:16.380
Oh, no. We're shooting our own.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.880
It's not good. It doesn't make sense why you're getting points.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:22.120
Do we have – they don't name our home country, do they?

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:25.040
They don't. I would assume it's the United States.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.160
Hell, yeah.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:30.300
So that was the place.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:33.040
The problem, though, is even worse, okay?

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:37.980
The terrorist-run country, Cantoon, has become completely power hungry.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:41.960
They're out of line. Their aim to take over the whole world.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.500
What is up with this fantasy of taking over the whole world?

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:49.140
Like – I mean it's what these games do.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:51.700
I mean that's usually what you're trying to fight against.

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:54.420
And then like that's one thing, right?

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:55.700
So they're going to take over the whole world.

00:15:55.700 --> 00:16:01.200
And then the manual like announces to you they're planning their attack right now.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.440
That's my favorite part of this.

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.480
Right as you read this page.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:09.120
The fact that it's like the second person like – are we scaring you yet?

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:12.180
Like you better start this game up now.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:15.300
Yeah, like it sounds like it's like a scary story being told to you like right now.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.360
I really appreciate that too.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:22.260
Even like the – you know, right as you read this page so there's little time left.

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:26.640
And it's like, okay, so why do I have like seven more paragraphs to go?

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:28.900
Like I don't know if I should read all this.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:34.520
So now that we have you really fired up, let's go over the controls and what the pickups do.

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:40.720
And also make sure you store the game cartridge in a very cool area.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:43.540
Don't let it get above 50 degrees Celsius.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:48.640
Yeah, and also this also has the whole like if it's on for two hours, pause for a little bit.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.100
Yeah, take a break, go outside.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:52.540
No, no, no. You guys remember what I'm talking about.

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:55.060
The one where it's like making up the go outside.

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:56.640
Yeah, this is a high precision game.

00:16:56.900 --> 00:17:01.480
And so like, you know, pause for 10 to 20 minutes after two hours of continuous gameplay.

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:04.260
Assuming somebody played this for two hours.

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:05.480
Two continuous hours.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:07.020
I don't know. I don't know about you guys.

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:12.540
But for me, it felt like if that's what helps this game perform, I should have maybe been pausing much more frequently.

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:15.220
Because not to go off the rails, but my game was not.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.460
My game was glitching out a lot.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:21.340
Yeah. I keep pausing and like it would fix itself a little bit.

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:23.800
But interesting. We're going to have to get more into that.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.980
One more snippet, though, from the manual that I really appreciated.

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:35.180
This one was cute. It says Tiger Heli is the result of a billion dollar defense project to create the ultimate stealth jet copter.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:36.920
Tiger Heli is turbo powered.

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:39.920
It's like a sales pitch.

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.840
Yeah, right? Like all of a sudden at the end, it's like there's the tagline.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.400
Does it have a Hemi? Tiger Heli.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:46.740
It's turbo powered.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:50.040
That's all the manual stuff I got.

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:51.860
Did anybody else find anything?

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:52.660
It's deep lore. No. Yeah.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:53.740
That's probably true.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:55.940
All right. Let's get into the gameplay then.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:18:00.480
So if this game can be summed up into, you know, a couple things.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:01.520
There's missiles.

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:04.560
There's enemies. There's other power ups.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:05.880
There's repetition.

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:07.780
And there's shmup.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:09.360
There's shmup.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.440
There's shmup to be done.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:16.680
What I liked at first about it was the power ups.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:18.520
Or if you call them power ups, you pick up a little.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:19.920
I would call them power ups.

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:22.780
Yeah, I guess so. Let's do it. You pick up little mini helicopters.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:26.820
Little baby copters. And that's based on like a power up thing that flashes different colors.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.680
You shoot it at the color that you want.

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.200
And there's like one.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:31.460
There's two options.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:36.660
Like one is copters that shoot sideways, which is nice, which I kind of preferred.

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.740
Or two copters on the side that shoot forward.

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:41.620
Well, they're more than just one.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.740
I'm sorry. Yeah. There are three options because the other one is bombs.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.020
Right. But I mean, as far as the helicopter.

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:50.840
Oh, OK. Yeah. And I thought that was like a really cool thing.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:53.100
It did like it did make the gameplay feel different and everything.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:57.140
But I feel like they're very they're pretty frequently available.

00:18:57.140 --> 00:19:01.680
And it just never just like you get those so early on and the game doesn't really change

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:03.120
too much after that.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:07.500
Like those are like the final changes to the game is like, oh, now you got these power ups.

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:14.500
I liked it because like, you know, I was I was trying to get my little mini copters and

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.340
I saw them as like my two boys.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:18.700
I wanted to protect my family.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.280
Did you name them? Lefty and righty.

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:22.960
Great. Very original.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:29.000
Yeah. Which one was which the the gray one was lefty and the gray one was righty.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:31.440
I avoided the right facing ones.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:35.220
Those should never like I just don't have a use for them.

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:39.600
I the only reason I like them is because when I in this game, I felt like anytime I did

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:43.740
hadn't shot something and got past it, I was like you have no choice but to dodge everything

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:46.380
that so at least if I was starting to pass something, I could still shoot it from the

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:51.280
side. One thing I want to point out is I'm going to agree with Joe there on the side thing.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:55.360
We always talk about how how power ups can be like great for these shmups.

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:58.720
And I think like Gradius was the best example of that.

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:02.280
But even like Stinger had some great options.

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:08.040
Yeah. But this one does have a lot of coverage if you do get all the power ups and don't let

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.480
anything get hit or taken down.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:15.580
I mean, you can have the copter shooting from the side, you can have multiple raise yourself

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:16.860
of like double power ups.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.240
This way you could be shooting like four lines or whatever.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:23.180
And so I think you can get like you could really like get a wide spread.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:28.080
And I like the side ones better because to Joe's point, like sometimes the tanks don't

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.520
necessarily appear from the very top.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.380
They might come in from the side or something like that.

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:36.460
So I appreciated like the option to do that because before previously we'd only ever had

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:39.160
like shooting directly ahead or shooting behind you.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:42.540
That's true. But I just like my little children.

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:43.500
Everybody has a preference.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:45.960
Yeah. OK. There's nothing wrong with lefty and righty.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:47.660
OK. They're fine.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:53.000
They're beautiful children. The bombs, though, on the other hand, not the best power up.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:58.160
But the one thing that was really cool about them was that if your opponents hit the bombs,

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:00.760
which are directly under you.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:05.500
It's like a free shield sort of thing. And also it'll trigger like anything near you to die.

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:06.560
Yeah. It's like an explosion.

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:11.500
Yeah. But you would think that if someone shot a bomb that was on you, you would blow up with

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.440
everything. Well, it looks like it's attached to your wing.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.080
Right? Right. Yeah.

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:21.980
I like to think of it more as they are shooting the hinge that drops the bomb and they're like,

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:24.480
oh, no. And then it falls on them.

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:25.680
Oh, OK. Right. Very precise.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.340
Very precise aim, but it just didn't precisely.

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:30.360
They precisely aimed at the wrong thing.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:35.200
Yeah. I like to think now, based on that, that we disguise our hinges to look like bombs and

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:36.300
our bombs to look like hinges.

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:39.840
So they shoot at what they think is the bomb, but that's actually the hinge.

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:44.640
Wow. That's beautiful. I don't think the gameplay design went that far, but it should have.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.040
Don't underestimate that. Maybe it's in the manual.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:47.620
Who knows? The manual covers a lot of things.

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:51.820
And then one thing I want to talk about with the enemies, does anybody else feel like they

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:53.760
require a pretty quick response time?

00:21:54.460 --> 00:22:01.340
I mean, there can be enough of them that you need to at least see ahead of time.

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:06.660
Like you need to anticipate where these slow moving projectiles are going.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:12.020
It's not like you don't need like the twitch reflexes, but if you start moving a little too

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:14.760
late, you will end up running into a missile.

00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:16.120
Yeah. It's a lot of dodging.

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:21.240
But like you said, you can plan out your dodging a little bit based on where the...

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:26.300
And specifically, if you don't have the other helicopters with you, if you're just the copter

00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:31.740
by yourself, I think once those tanks get past you and now they're behind you, it makes

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:33.420
the game like twice as hard.

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:37.020
Yeah. Because now you have no option but just dodge until they go off screen.

00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:38.300
Right. And that's when they give up, I guess.

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:39.420
Yeah, it's not very intimidating. Yeah, yeah.

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:42.040
Well, they have to give up at some point, right?

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:43.780
I guess, yeah. It's like the laws of video games.

00:22:43.940 --> 00:22:45.360
Yeah, a helicopter will be faster.

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:46.980
I imagine that's a tank.

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:49.940
Right. Do I have anything?

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:51.180
Oh, yeah. And then repetition.

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:53.620
I guess what I meant by that was just the one music track.

00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:56.680
Well, this is just something that keeps happening.

00:22:56.920 --> 00:23:04.140
Like, all of these developers can only be bothered to compose one or two five-bar songs.

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:05.480
They got four stages.

00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:07.100
You couldn't just design four tracks?

00:23:07.100 --> 00:23:08.680
Well, they do have two tracks.

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:13.820
One is like a very modified version of the original track when you have power-up.

00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:15.840
I'm glad you said that. I'm glad you said that because I didn't notice.

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:20.940
Yeah. It's like the same tempo and everything.

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:23.480
It's just like different. The notes are like changed up a little bit.

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:26.580
It's a little bit more uplifting.

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:31.280
Yes. But it lasts, I think, the whole time you have any side helicopters.

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:32.800
Little boys. Yes.

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:34.140
Or my boys.

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:37.340
Right. Any of Sean's boys is what they're officially called now.

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:42.900
My sons. What you shoot, you think that's missiles or you think those are just like ammo?

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:44.620
Like guns? Ammo.

00:23:45.460 --> 00:23:47.400
You're just shooting raw guns at people.

00:23:49.460 --> 00:23:50.640
No, I meant like bullets.

00:23:52.440 --> 00:23:54.460
I guess I would think they're missiles.

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:55.580
I would say missiles, right?

00:23:55.580 --> 00:23:56.980
They come pretty infrequently.

00:23:57.140 --> 00:23:58.020
It's not like a machine gun.

00:23:58.020 --> 00:23:59.760
You don't destroy a tank with bullets either.

00:23:59.940 --> 00:24:01.600
You know, you kind of got to be shooting missiles.

00:24:01.820 --> 00:24:07.740
Well, technically, there are bullets that can go through tanks.

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:10.200
But I think they're missiles.

00:24:10.500 --> 00:24:11.800
Can you talk like that for the rest of the podcast?

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:13.960
Yeah. Okay.

00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:19.480
And the only thing that was interesting to note about the missiles is that they shoot exactly half a screen.

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:23.400
Well, because you're shooting them at the ground.

00:24:23.440 --> 00:24:25.160
And that's where it hits the ground.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:26.340
At exactly half.

00:24:26.540 --> 00:24:28.900
Like it takes half a screen for the curvature of the earth.

00:24:29.040 --> 00:24:31.880
No, no. You're going 45 degree angle.

00:24:32.140 --> 00:24:33.540
Okay. You don't have to talk like that anymore.

00:24:33.700 --> 00:24:34.560
Oh, okay. Sorry, Mike.

00:24:34.780 --> 00:24:35.600
I didn't want to.

00:24:35.820 --> 00:24:36.800
Yeah. But I don't want to.

00:24:36.800 --> 00:24:37.920
You didn't want to disappoint.

00:24:38.060 --> 00:24:43.040
Exactly. The thing I liked about the half a screen length thing is that it's very precise.

00:24:43.720 --> 00:24:46.860
Like it was even mentioned on like game FAQs or something like that.

00:24:46.960 --> 00:24:49.400
It's like, when is that now it's going to become useful to me?

00:24:49.580 --> 00:24:53.760
Like, oh, I'm not. You know, like that guy is at 75% of the screen and I'm back here.

00:24:53.920 --> 00:24:54.900
Like. You mean in real life?

00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:58.620
No. Yeah.

00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:00.860
I guess you could think like, oh, I'll buy a longer TV.

00:25:00.860 --> 00:25:05.180
Like if I buy a more vertical TV, they'll shoot further.

00:25:05.620 --> 00:25:12.080
I thought you were talking about how this game would wrongly educate you to think that nobody

00:25:12.080 --> 00:25:14.620
could shoot you if they were more than half the screen length away.

00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:16.260
No, gotcha. No, I wasn't thinking that.

00:25:16.380 --> 00:25:20.860
Just like how I don't think that, um, like in Hogan's alley, that that's how they actually

00:25:20.860 --> 00:25:22.240
train the FBI agents.

00:25:22.240 --> 00:25:25.200
Wait, I thought they just use a copy of Hogan's alley.

00:25:25.380 --> 00:25:26.320
To this day. Yes.

00:25:27.680 --> 00:25:30.400
Yep. Um, that was in Comey's biography, right?

00:25:30.880 --> 00:25:34.420
Talked about. Comey's alley.

00:25:34.940 --> 00:25:36.160
The sequel. Um, okay.

00:25:36.900 --> 00:25:40.360
And then, uh, so I think that's, that covers it for me for gameplay.

00:25:40.640 --> 00:25:42.720
Anybody else got anything on thoughts on gameplay?

00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:45.560
I mean, the enemies don't really change up that much.

00:25:45.660 --> 00:25:50.220
If there's one thing I loved about Stinger, the other episode we just did was that the enemy

00:25:50.220 --> 00:25:54.460
variety was like every single stage was different and there was like seven different enemies

00:25:54.460 --> 00:25:56.000
to go through. Coat hangers.

00:25:56.240 --> 00:25:57.140
Yeah. Coat hangers. Yeah.

00:25:57.200 --> 00:25:58.580
There were no coat hangers in this game.

00:25:58.760 --> 00:26:00.400
So there's no way it could be essential.

00:26:00.720 --> 00:26:03.080
That blue bubbles. Um, oh yeah.

00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:04.140
They're wearing saxophones.

00:26:04.280 --> 00:26:05.300
Yeah. It's disappointing.

00:26:05.600 --> 00:26:07.620
Um, it's, it's a little too grounded in reality.

00:26:07.780 --> 00:26:08.780
There isn't enough deep lore.

00:26:09.020 --> 00:26:15.040
Yep. So my only thought about gameplay, which I don't think is going to apply to everybody, is my personal

00:26:15.040 --> 00:26:16.000
experience with gameplay.

00:26:16.300 --> 00:26:20.100
Uh, a lot of times I started getting a lot of strange graphical.

00:26:20.220 --> 00:26:21.260
Glitches going on.

00:26:21.360 --> 00:26:26.860
And I don't think any of them really affected like what was on screen, but it affected sometimes

00:26:26.860 --> 00:26:28.420
what I could see. Sometimes I disappeared.

00:26:28.500 --> 00:26:32.060
Like I couldn't see myself for like, for like five seconds.

00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:38.200
Uh, and then other times textures, if you want to call them that, just like whatever you

00:26:38.200 --> 00:26:43.120
call them, the ground or whatever, like green or whatever, like just one color gray would

00:26:43.120 --> 00:26:44.140
just suddenly be numbers.

00:26:44.140 --> 00:26:49.300
Like, I don't know if you have like a pirated copy or something.

00:26:49.300 --> 00:26:50.660
It was just like glitching out.

00:26:50.880 --> 00:26:55.020
Like, have you ever, you've never had that where like, uh, you boot it up and then halfway

00:26:55.020 --> 00:26:57.660
through, halfway through like an NES game, suddenly weird.

00:26:58.100 --> 00:27:00.120
Uh, yeah. Glitchy elements pop up.

00:27:00.340 --> 00:27:01.320
No, for sure. I mean, you know, yeah.

00:27:01.520 --> 00:27:04.580
So, I mean. So that happened and I thought I was going to have to start over, but then I just kind

00:27:04.580 --> 00:27:09.280
of kept like fighting through it and eventually it would just kind of like pop back into normal.

00:27:09.440 --> 00:27:11.200
Yeah. You might've had like missing no pop up.

00:27:11.580 --> 00:27:15.880
Yeah. I mean like that happens with cartridges when they're like loose and out of place.

00:27:15.880 --> 00:27:19.940
Like you can do some cool stuff with, um, I think it's Super Mario World where you play

00:27:19.940 --> 00:27:20.960
around with the, that's Super Nintendo.

00:27:20.960 --> 00:27:24.740
I know. But like when you play around with the cartridge on that, like you can get graphical sprites

00:27:24.740 --> 00:27:26.440
to like pop up in the game.

00:27:26.460 --> 00:27:28.380
Playing with like half in, like on an angle.

00:27:28.700 --> 00:27:31.320
Yep. There's a lot of like, remember PlayStation 1.

00:27:31.480 --> 00:27:34.040
I mean, we're definitely not, we don't talk about that that often, but like.

00:27:34.560 --> 00:27:36.320
Take out the CD. You can just take out the CD.

00:27:36.600 --> 00:27:37.920
Change the music. Yeah. Change the music.

00:27:37.920 --> 00:27:41.400
It's like the game's still running somehow and it's like, what's going on?

00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:43.160
Very confusing.

00:27:43.520 --> 00:27:45.600
Um, thought I dreamt that as a kid actually one time.

00:27:45.780 --> 00:27:46.660
It happened. It's Rizit.

00:27:47.140 --> 00:27:48.520
Um, oh.

00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:50.000
I dreamt that.

00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:54.980
Uh, also there is a way to get, um, continues in this game.

00:27:55.280 --> 00:27:59.600
Uh, you can get an extra continue on your game over by holding down A and B during the

00:27:59.600 --> 00:28:04.940
game over screen. I know that we always talk about like continue systems and like how they work and stuff.

00:28:05.200 --> 00:28:06.520
It wasn't that rewarding. It's not that satisfying.

00:28:06.520 --> 00:28:07.940
And I don't like the fact that it's hidden.

00:28:08.120 --> 00:28:09.940
And is that just once or is that?

00:28:10.100 --> 00:28:11.100
I think it's just once. Okay.

00:28:11.260 --> 00:28:14.260
Yeah. I mean, it's not that hard to accrue extra lives.

00:28:14.440 --> 00:28:18.820
Like you just, there are those bonus blocks that if you get 10 of them, you get an extra

00:28:18.820 --> 00:28:19.640
life. Yeah.

00:28:19.700 --> 00:28:21.500
And I think there's, there's a couple of other ways.

00:28:21.580 --> 00:28:23.340
There's like 20,000 points.

00:28:23.720 --> 00:28:26.520
20,000 and 80,000. Yep. And that's like 20,000 is pretty fast.

00:28:26.740 --> 00:28:28.800
Yeah. So I mean like the game is generous.

00:28:29.040 --> 00:28:30.720
It's not, I'm not saying it's hard.

00:28:31.460 --> 00:28:32.560
I'm asking, is it fun?

00:28:32.820 --> 00:28:34.380
Like, yeah, but we'll get to that.

00:28:34.700 --> 00:28:37.020
Yeah. Bye.

00:29:04.880 --> 00:29:08.960
Bye.!! Thank you.

00:29:37.080 --> 00:29:40.260
We can talk about some sequels and spinoffs.

00:29:40.380 --> 00:29:43.900
Can't wait. Were you expecting sequels and spinoffs from Tiger Heli?

00:29:44.080 --> 00:29:48.380
I mean, I'm expecting there to be sequels and spinoffs of every game we play now.

00:29:48.580 --> 00:29:59.560
Like, apparently every half-assed game that we play has 13 further entries into the 2000s with anthology editions.

00:29:59.560 --> 00:30:00.880
And I'm just going to stop talking.

00:30:00.880 --> 00:30:08.000
It's okay, because I was surprised to find out that there were two sequels, only two, to Tiger Heli.

00:30:08.120 --> 00:30:12.500
Because they don't have anything in name with Tiger Heli.

00:30:12.580 --> 00:30:14.680
And they're actually pretty well-received games.

00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:19.820
The Twin Cobra series is somehow connected to...

00:30:19.820 --> 00:30:22.440
And I guess maybe it's because they're just also made by Toplan.

00:30:22.440 --> 00:30:25.000
And they also feature helicopters as the main thing.

00:30:25.060 --> 00:30:27.800
They're really into helicopters. But, like, yeah, they're just loving helicopters.

00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:29.820
And I mean, like, look, I'm all for variety, right?

00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:31.380
So far, think about it.

00:30:31.520 --> 00:30:37.760
We've had a cartoon spaceship, a real spaceship, not to be confused with fake spaceships.

00:30:38.600 --> 00:30:40.320
Wait, why didn't we talk about...

00:30:40.320 --> 00:30:42.900
Wasn't Scoon, technically, like a schmuck?

00:30:42.900 --> 00:30:43.940
Yeah, I guess so, right?

00:30:44.060 --> 00:30:45.400
Two? We've had a submarine?

00:30:45.740 --> 00:30:49.140
Yeah, I think they're... At this point, do you want to call Star Voyager a schmuck?

00:30:49.140 --> 00:30:50.440
No, that is not a schmuck.

00:30:50.640 --> 00:30:52.120
That is a simulation.

00:30:53.960 --> 00:30:54.780
That's a something.

00:30:55.120 --> 00:30:58.160
Anyway, to get back to the Twin Cobra games, they're very well-received games.

00:30:58.880 --> 00:31:01.480
And so Twin Cobra 1 will come to the NES.

00:31:01.480 --> 00:31:02.680
We will get a chance at it.

00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:05.920
So if everybody can just remember when we finally get to 1990.

00:31:06.120 --> 00:31:08.680
We're currently in 1987, for those keeping score.

00:31:08.920 --> 00:31:13.500
If we can just remember Tiger Heli as we're playing Twin Cobra,

00:31:13.660 --> 00:31:18.040
I'm sure we'll be like, wow, look at how much advancements there's been in three years' time.

00:31:19.180 --> 00:31:20.240
So that's just...

00:31:20.240 --> 00:31:21.880
Or not. There may be no change.

00:31:22.180 --> 00:31:25.040
Yeah. It's interesting to note that that one is well-received, though.

00:31:25.180 --> 00:31:29.340
And my understanding is that Tiger Heli back in the day was well-received on arcades.

00:31:29.560 --> 00:31:32.340
Not necessarily the NES port, but the arcade version.

00:31:32.560 --> 00:31:33.500
Yeah, I haven't really heard...

00:31:33.500 --> 00:31:41.860
Because I did look up reviews by people of this time, not back in the 80s.

00:31:42.320 --> 00:31:43.500
And it's still...

00:31:43.500 --> 00:31:44.600
People still like the game.

00:31:44.620 --> 00:31:46.140
Yeah, I saw a lot of positive reviews, too.

00:31:46.300 --> 00:31:49.040
Yeah. Yeah, I think we're just expecting a little something more.

00:31:49.140 --> 00:31:50.780
We've played some great games recently.

00:31:51.380 --> 00:31:55.840
And then Twin Cobra 2, which would obviously be the sequel to Twin Cobra,

00:31:56.140 --> 00:31:57.380
is also in that franchise.

00:31:57.380 --> 00:32:00.920
And it was released in 1996 for the arcade and Sega Saturn.

00:32:02.240 --> 00:32:03.340
Maybe the PlayStation?

00:32:03.620 --> 00:32:04.560
But don't quote me on that.

00:32:04.620 --> 00:32:07.100
I think the PlayStation got a compilation release of the two of them.

00:32:07.400 --> 00:32:09.920
Anyway, that was also developed by Topeland.

00:32:10.140 --> 00:32:13.140
But they closed in 1994, if you remember from my development history.

00:32:13.680 --> 00:32:17.520
So Taito allowed their offshoot company, Takumi, to finish.

00:32:17.820 --> 00:32:22.300
So that's kind of cool that some of the designers from Topeland, after the company dissolved,

00:32:22.720 --> 00:32:24.500
went on to still finish one of their products.

00:32:24.820 --> 00:32:27.200
Does Takumi still exist?

00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:28.980
I don't know. I never heard of Takumi.

00:32:29.160 --> 00:32:31.740
Yeah, they probably also declared bankruptcy at one point.

00:32:31.740 --> 00:32:34.780
They're like shoes that are from Adidas that have Takumi in them.

00:32:35.040 --> 00:32:36.940
Like, that's the name. They're like Onitsuka Tigers?

00:32:37.400 --> 00:32:38.420
No, they're not.

00:32:38.520 --> 00:32:39.640
But those are cool shoes.

00:32:39.880 --> 00:32:41.640
And there's a whole story about that, actually.

00:32:42.060 --> 00:32:43.200
We're going to get that later.

00:32:43.380 --> 00:32:44.520
Yeah, you'll get that whole story.

00:32:45.040 --> 00:32:49.740
I think if no one else has anything to add, we're going to go right into the Essential Games list.

00:32:53.100 --> 00:32:54.640
Sean, you're on a desert island.

00:32:55.360 --> 00:32:57.680
You only get to take 30 games.

00:32:58.300 --> 00:32:59.680
They are the Essential Games.

00:33:00.420 --> 00:33:01.940
Is this one coming with you?

00:33:02.600 --> 00:33:06.100
Now, do I have a power source and a television set?

00:33:06.280 --> 00:33:07.800
No. You just get to look at them.

00:33:09.260 --> 00:33:12.480
And they don't come with the manuals, so you can't vote based on how cool the manuals are.

00:33:12.480 --> 00:33:15.060
Or how much paper you have for starting fires.

00:33:15.200 --> 00:33:19.540
So they have to be just entirely based on the box art?

00:33:19.600 --> 00:33:20.880
Like, that's entirely on?

00:33:20.880 --> 00:33:22.080
No, no, no. Okay, okay, okay, okay.

00:33:22.460 --> 00:33:23.800
The Essential Games list is...

00:33:24.420 --> 00:33:30.400
Yeah, exactly. It's that thing we do where we look at the games no longer as they were when they first came out,

00:33:30.500 --> 00:33:31.520
but how they hold up today.

00:33:31.520 --> 00:33:32.520
How they look on a desert island.

00:33:32.820 --> 00:33:33.780
Right. No, no, no, no.

00:33:33.860 --> 00:33:35.280
How they play today.

00:33:35.280 --> 00:33:36.820
The desert island thing is just implied.

00:33:37.100 --> 00:33:38.840
Like, we don't usually say it, but...

00:33:38.840 --> 00:33:41.640
But we still don't have a power source to play the games.

00:33:41.840 --> 00:33:43.680
Right. It's always been about a desert island.

00:33:45.360 --> 00:33:47.380
The podcast has always been...

00:33:47.380 --> 00:33:49.840
Basically, that's the whole plan, is that at the end of the podcast,

00:33:49.920 --> 00:33:52.900
after we do 716 episodes or however many games there are...

00:33:52.900 --> 00:33:54.160
We throw them all into the ocean.

00:33:54.440 --> 00:33:59.120
No, we basically, like, land on a desert island and live there for the rest of our lives

00:33:59.120 --> 00:34:00.760
with just the games we've considered essential.

00:34:00.820 --> 00:34:01.740
I thought you guys knew this.

00:34:01.820 --> 00:34:03.100
We signed a contract at the beginning.

00:34:03.200 --> 00:34:04.960
I just thought that goes without saying.

00:34:05.740 --> 00:34:07.920
I wasn't aware, and I'm suing you.

00:34:08.060 --> 00:34:10.040
So what's your vote then, Sean, for this?

00:34:10.280 --> 00:34:11.460
Now knowing what you know.

00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:14.420
To be honest, like, this game isn't bad.

00:34:14.820 --> 00:34:16.420
It's, um...

00:34:16.420 --> 00:34:23.340
It does a couple cool things to at least keep it interesting with the way that the power-ups work,

00:34:23.420 --> 00:34:24.620
but it's been done before.

00:34:25.200 --> 00:34:27.060
I'm not a big fan of helicopters.

00:34:27.060 --> 00:34:29.360
I'm not a big fan of breaking the Geneva Convention.

00:34:29.360 --> 00:34:35.560
I don't know, like, why they couldn't make music for each different level,

00:34:36.560 --> 00:34:39.580
but, you know, I did like blowing up the houses.

00:34:40.820 --> 00:34:42.120
That was a slip.

00:34:42.280 --> 00:34:43.340
I didn't mean to say that.

00:34:44.320 --> 00:34:47.980
That's okay. You've said some more questionable things on this podcast than that.

00:34:49.160 --> 00:34:50.860
It's not an essential game.

00:34:50.940 --> 00:34:54.140
We've been spoiled by Stinger and Gradius.

00:34:55.340 --> 00:34:57.640
I don't want to see more shmups.

00:34:57.780 --> 00:34:58.760
I'm getting sick of shmups.

00:34:59.300 --> 00:35:00.440
Okay. Joe?

00:35:01.580 --> 00:35:02.680
Yeah, I think...

00:35:02.680 --> 00:35:04.720
I can't remember what game we were talking about.

00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:08.180
I think I've said this before, that I feel like we were past this.

00:35:08.500 --> 00:35:10.640
Like, it didn't do anything particularly wrong,

00:35:11.200 --> 00:35:16.200
but I just feel like there's nothing wrong with a game being simple and fun,

00:35:16.200 --> 00:35:21.020
but I think this was simple and just didn't have enough to it to keep my interest.

00:35:21.320 --> 00:35:25.320
So I thought it was okay.

00:35:25.520 --> 00:35:27.520
I don't know if I would even really give it a play, to be honest.

00:35:29.200 --> 00:35:32.000
Just because I'm also kind of bored with this type of game.

00:35:32.780 --> 00:35:35.140
Yeah. I think you both hit the nails on the head here.

00:35:35.740 --> 00:35:39.200
Sean, you said something that I was going to go off of, but then Joe said it even better.

00:35:39.740 --> 00:35:40.740
It's okay. Oh, I'm sorry.

00:35:41.080 --> 00:35:42.300
No, no, no. I meant like you said.

00:35:42.460 --> 00:35:43.860
No, I get it. You said it's not bad.

00:35:43.920 --> 00:35:46.080
Yeah, it's better than me with words.

00:35:46.240 --> 00:35:47.300
It's not a bad game.

00:35:48.080 --> 00:35:52.600
It's okay. And that's not the criteria for the Essential Games list.

00:35:52.840 --> 00:35:56.260
I'm not telling you that if you like this game, you need to reevaluate your choices,

00:35:56.260 --> 00:35:59.020
because it's totally fine to like this game.

00:35:59.180 --> 00:36:03.220
I think the three of us took away that we don't like it, and we're never going to revisit it.

00:36:03.360 --> 00:36:07.320
Yeah. I like PsyOps on Xbox, but you don't have to like PsyOps on Xbox.

00:36:07.580 --> 00:36:08.540
No one gets that.

00:36:08.800 --> 00:36:13.300
Okay. It sounds like some buried stuff for you, though.

00:36:13.520 --> 00:36:14.660
You know what? I like the game.

00:36:14.840 --> 00:36:17.360
Yeah. Did your mom question you liking PsyOps?

00:36:17.440 --> 00:36:19.140
She came in your room one time and was like, PsyOps?

00:36:19.260 --> 00:36:22.000
You're playing PsyOps? It's just like the deep psychological scar.

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:23.960
They had a music video that you could watch.

00:36:24.140 --> 00:36:26.920
It was from the band Cold, and it was about the game.

00:36:27.280 --> 00:36:29.500
And the music video had footage from the game in it.

00:36:29.720 --> 00:36:31.400
Okay. The post show will be about PsyOps.

00:36:32.320 --> 00:36:33.500
Okay. So stick around for that.

00:36:33.500 --> 00:36:39.940
In the meantime, the Essential Games list has officially been voted no for Tiger Heli.

00:36:40.840 --> 00:36:44.060
What will happen to Twin Cobra remains to be seen.

00:36:44.060 --> 00:36:45.840
We'll find out in a few hundred episodes.

00:36:45.900 --> 00:36:47.400
Yes, in 150 episodes.

00:36:47.760 --> 00:36:50.980
But that is definitely all the time we have for this episode of Nostalgia.

00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:54.960
Don't leave just yet because I think that we have some great news for you.

00:36:57.220 --> 00:36:58.500
Sean, take it away.

00:36:58.980 --> 00:37:01.060
So we are going public.

00:37:01.060 --> 00:37:09.340
We have an IPO in April of 2020, and we hope that you will buy our stock.

00:37:10.020 --> 00:37:13.960
We are doing an initial pricing of $21 per share.

00:37:14.580 --> 00:37:18.660
I don't know if that's how it works, but we're hoping that the SEC lets us do that.

00:37:18.940 --> 00:37:23.060
So if you don't have a brokerage account, get one.

00:37:23.200 --> 00:37:26.140
All certificates will be printed out on Crayola Paint.

00:37:26.140 --> 00:37:32.520
Yeah, we can send you physical stock so that people can't steal them.

00:37:32.760 --> 00:37:36.480
Yep. And they'll also come with a little mini message from Sean.

00:37:36.820 --> 00:37:38.300
Yeah. Yep. Which is secret.

00:37:38.480 --> 00:37:39.960
Don't say it now. It's all personalized.

00:37:40.140 --> 00:37:41.440
Yep. Joe, any announcements?

00:37:41.620 --> 00:37:43.700
I just got to say, that was some pretty good improv.

00:37:43.940 --> 00:37:47.660
I thought I was going to throw you under the bus there.

00:37:47.660 --> 00:37:48.500
What do you mean improv?

00:37:48.500 --> 00:37:55.340
This is the point where most shows push where to find them, and here we are just posting made-up news.

00:37:58.160 --> 00:38:00.620
Don't miss the Nostalgia Cover Band.

00:38:00.900 --> 00:38:05.680
They're the band that plays at a bar in your local neighborhood every Thursday.

00:38:06.340 --> 00:38:08.380
In every local neighborhood in the world.

00:38:08.580 --> 00:38:12.800
Well, each one of them has one, and they basically do impressions of us.

00:38:12.800 --> 00:38:15.880
It's a franchise. In fact, that's a good thing.

00:38:15.880 --> 00:38:22.460
We are currently not booked in Pittsburgh, so if anybody in Pittsburgh wants to start a Nostalgia Cover Band,

00:38:22.560 --> 00:38:27.420
where you basically just go on stage, and instead of playing music, you just do an impression of us.

00:38:27.500 --> 00:38:30.440
Really, anyone who talks about video games is kind of impersonating us.

00:38:30.600 --> 00:38:38.100
If you have one of those in your hometown, we have the right to the talking about video games.

00:38:38.300 --> 00:38:43.260
I have sent IGN a cease and desist for most of the content that they've been putting out,

00:38:43.260 --> 00:38:47.480
because essentially they're not following the Nostalgia Cover Band rules.

00:38:48.500 --> 00:38:51.100
So I'm waiting for Pierre Schneider to get back to me on that.

00:38:51.340 --> 00:38:52.160
Pierre Schneider?

00:38:52.380 --> 00:38:54.060
The co-founder of IGN.

00:38:54.140 --> 00:38:55.660
I don't know who IGN Man is.

00:38:55.840 --> 00:38:57.000
I thought it was Pierre Schneider. Is it Pierre?

00:38:57.120 --> 00:38:58.560
